	</item>
	<item>
		<title>It does not have to mean anything</title>
		<link>/one-charm/</link>
		<pubDate>2026-08-30 12:00:00</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[admin]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">/?p=109</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p class="prose__lead">On charms, meaning, and the freedom of just liking the look of a small bee.</p>
  <h2 class="prose__sub">The meaning problem</h2>
  <p>Charm jewelry has spent a long time being sold as a memory system. A charm for the trip, a charm for the birth, a charm for the year everything changed. That is lovely and it is also a lot of pressure to put on a small piece of enamel.</p>
  <h2 class="prose__sub">The alternative</h2>
  <p>Our charms come with no story attached. Pick the mushroom because you like mushrooms. Pick the bow because it is a good bow. Put six on a bracelet that have nothing to do with each other and let that be the whole point.</p>
  <p>At $12 you can afford to choose badly, which is exactly the freedom that a meaningful charm never gives you.</p>]]></content:encoded>
		<excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[]]></excerpt:encoded>
		<wp:post_id>109</wp:post_id>
		<wp:post_date><![CDATA[2026-08-30 12:00:00]]></wp:post_date>
